sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor B as Buyer
    participant Web as Storefront
    participant API as API
    participant DB as Postgres
    participant W as Worker (orders queue)
    participant S as Scheduler (lisskins.snapshot, lisskins.reconcile)
    participant LS as LIS-SKINS

    loop every 5 min (lisskins.snapshot)
        S->>LS: GET market_export_json/api_csgo_full.json (~855 MB, streamed, no key)
        Note over S: keep instant, unlocked lots; map to the catalogue; 10 cheapest per item
        S->>DB: pricing lock → upsert / delete lisskins_offers, roll up onto skin_items, lisskins_state, reprice
        Note over S,DB: under half of the last tick's lots → refused, nothing written
    end

    B->>Web: opens an item page
    Web->>API: GET /skins/{slug}/listings
    API->>DB: lisskins_offers (no external call; stale > 20 min = none), merged with Skinslink by price
    API-->>Web: offers (ls:<id>, sl:<id>)

    B->>Web: picks an offer (ls:<id>)
    Web->>API: POST /orders {slug, listing_id: "ls:…", price_uzs} + Idempotency-Key
    API->>DB: read the item, rules, rate, stored offers; end the transaction
    API->>LS: GET /market/check-availability?ids[]=<id> (4 s, ≤ 100/min, 120 s breaker)
    alt available
        Note over API: the live price replaces the snapshot's (dearer > 2 % → price_changed)
    else gone
        Note over API: offer_gone with next_offer (never a replacement)
    else no answer
        Note over API: the snapshot price stands (the worker's max_price guards)
    end
    API->>DB: insert order (source = lisskins, offer_id, cost_units) pending
    API-->>Web: 201 OrderOut
    B->>API: POST /orders/{number}/pay (balance or a kassa)
    API->>DB: paid + NOTIFY orders

    DB-->>W: NOTIFY orders
    W->>DB: drain_paid: claim → buying; lisskins_purchases (custom_id = order id, buy_pending)
    W->>DB: take the lease (source = lisskins), read the snapshot
    W->>LS: POST /market/buy {ids: [id], partner, token, max_price, custom_id} (no lock held)
    alt processing / wait_accept
        W->>DB: lock order → purchase, record purchase_id + status, buy_pending = false
    else custom_id_already_exists
        W->>LS: GET /market/info?custom_ids[]=… → adopt the stored purchase
    else skins_unavailable / price higher than max_price
        W->>DB: failed + refund to balance (sold_out), no other offer bought
    else trade-link code
        W->>DB: failed + refund to balance (invalid_trade_link)
    else insufficient_funds
        W->>DB: failed + refund to balance (source_low_balance)
    else 401 / 403
        W->>DB: attention source_forbidden, buy_pending kept
    else timeout / 5xx / network
        W->>DB: buy_unconfirmed_at (the reconcile asks market/info under the same custom_id)
    end
    W->>DB: release the lease

    loop every 30 s (lisskins.reconcile)
        S->>DB: pending buys (≤ 20) → the buy path above
        S->>DB: open purchases + delivered ones in trade protection (≤ 200)
        S->>LS: GET /market/info?custom_ids[]=…&custom_ids[]=… (one call)
        S->>DB: lock order → purchase, apply each status
        alt wait_accept with an offer
            S->>DB: buying → trade_sent (offer URL, letter, nudge)
        else accepted
            S->>DB: trade_sent → delivered (then polled every 10 min for 8 days)
        else return before acceptance
            S->>DB: returned + refund (not_accepted), or failed + refund (trade_create_error)
        else return with rollback_* / after delivery
            S->>DB: attention rolled_back
        else not found, unconfirmed past order_unconfirmed_minutes
            S->>DB: buy_pending again → bought under the same custom_id
        end
    end
